But the preceding commit 5dff09c040c0c63c56d9794e35c96dde4822ae4e introducing `SplitLines` creates a smaller-scale version of the original problem because `SplitLines` is *not* safe to use with untrusted input. Would suggest fixing this by just dropping commit 5dff09c040c0c63c56d9794e35c96dde4822ae4e and simplifying the PR. `SplitLines` was intended to make log output look a little nicer in some cases by preserving newlines, but I think your example shows it is not actually safe in practice and not worth keeping.
